# New
- Matrices can now be initialized with arrays.
```c++
Matrix A = {
    {1,2,3},
    {4,5,6},
    {7,8,9}
};
A.print();
// 3x3 matrix
// | 1 2 3 |
// | 4 5 6 |
// | 7 8 9 |
```
- Generic matrices now can easily be initialized with the la::generic(i, j) and la::ones(i, j) functions.
```c++
Matrix A = la::generic(2,2);
A.print();
// 2x2 matrix
// | 1 2 |
// | 3 4 |
Matrix B = la::ones(3,1);
B.print();
// 3x1 matrix
// | 1 |
// | 1 |
// | 1 |
```
- Similarly, identity matrices can be initialized with the la::identity(i) function.
```c++
Matrix A = la::identity(3);
A.print();
// 3x3 matrix
// | 1 0 0 |
// | 0 1 0 |
// | 0 0 1 |
```

## Operations
 - Submatrix
```c++
Matrix A = la::generic(3,3);
Matrix B = A.submat(0,0);
B.print();
// 2x2 matrix
// | 5.000000 6.000000 |
// | 8.000000 9.000000 |
```
 - In-place minus
 ```c++
Matrix A = la::generic(1,2);
Matrix B = la::ones(1,2);
A -= B;
A.print();
// 1x2 matrix
// | 0.000000 1.000000 |
```
 - Fill
```c++
Matrix A(3,4);
A.fill(2.5f);
A.print();
// 3x4 matrix
// | 2.500000 2.500000 2.500000 2.500000 |
// | 2.500000 2.500000 2.500000 2.500000 |
// | 2.500000 2.500000 2.500000 2.500000 |
```
 - Build matrices from vectors
```c++
std::vector<std::vector<float>> x = {
   {4, 3, 2, 7},
   {1, 0, 5, 8}
};
Matrix A = la::fromVector(x);
A.print();
// | 4.000000 3.000000 2.000000 7.000000 |
// | 1.000000 0.000000 5.000000 8.000000 |
```
 - Transpose and in-place transpose
```c++
Matrix A = la::generic(2,3);
A.print();
A.transpose_();
A.print();
Matrix B = A.transpose();
B.print();

// 2x3 matrix
// | 1.000000 2.000000 4.000000 |
// | 4.000000 5.000000 6.000000 |
// 3x2 matrix
// | 1.000000 4.000000 |
// | 2.000000 5.000000 |
// | 4.000000 6.000000 |
// 2x3 matrix
// | 1.000000 2.000000 4.000000 |
// | 4.000000 5.000000 6.000000 |
```
 - Trace
```c++
Matrix A = la::generic(6,6);
Matrix B(4,4);
Matrix C = la::identity(9);
*B.at(2,2) = 5;

printf("tr(A) = %.2f, tr(B) = %.2f, tr(C) = %.2f\n",
       A.trace(), B.trace(), C.trace());
// tr(A) = 111.00, tr(B) = 5.00, tr(C) = 9.00
```
